  "notes": "An intransitive verb meaning for a dark or closed period to end and give way to what follows. Not to be confused with {開|あ}ける (to open) or {空|あ}ける (to empty, to vacate), which are transitive.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {夜|よる}が{明|あ}ける: dawn breaks\n- {年|とし}が{明|あ}ける: a new year begins\n- {梅雨|つゆ}が{明|あ}ける: the rainy season ends\n- {喪|も}が{明|あ}ける: the mourning period ends\n- {夜|よ}{明|あ}け: dawn, daybreak (noun form)\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nThis {明|あ}ける is intransitive — the period or darkness itself ends. There is no direct transitive counterpart with this meaning.\n\nCONTRAST WITH OTHER あける:\n- {開|あ}ける: to open (a door, a lid) — transitive\n- {空|あ}ける: to empty, to vacate (a room, a seat) — transitive\n- {明|あ}ける: to dawn, to end (a period) — intransitive (this entry)",
